{
 "$comment": "First pass, picked from 240 px thumbnails of the 317 lightbox shots (Apr 15 2025); re-picked for the right side at full resolution on Oct 19 2026. Each pick is confirmed again when its frame goes through the clean-up (docs/brief/07-photography.md). Angles: A1 front, A2 three-quarter, A3 side, A4 top-down, A5 inside, A6 GCD detail, H landscape hero. 'sides' gives the wearer's side each pick shows ('front' when no temple face is seen). The GCD is on the right side only (00-decisions.md #31), so A2, A6 and the hero use right-side shots wherever the shoot has them; A3 keeps a true left profile where the shoot has no right one. How to tell the side: on an outside view, the front at the image right with the temple running left is the right side. Views from behind flip that rule, so they are checked by the hinge hardware (it sits on the inside) and by the old print reading the right way round (it sits on the outside).",
